From f3ee24c9bb359588c2c14af44f93e83084ffb9f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:02:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution settings: review fixes, copies of the material
 arrays, behaviour libraries for both processors

Fixes of an independent review of the execution settings:

- with `--execution`, the behaviours are integrated by batches by default
  (the libraries generated by the generic-parallel interface for the host
  were refused by the default `PointByPoint`, while the check accepted
  them);
- a device which is not a GPU (debug device of MFEM, accepted with
  `--execution cpu`) integrates the behaviours on the CPU;
- with `--execution`, the environment variables placing the computations
  (`MFEM_MGIS_DEVICE`, `MFEM_MGIS_HYPRE_ON_HOST`,
  `MFEM_MGIS_BEHAVIOUR_INTEGRATION`, `MFEM_MGIS_*_COMPUTATION`) are ignored,
  with a warning printed once, instead of contradicting the option or
  overriding it; the options `--hypre-on-host`, `--no-hypre-on-host` and
  `--device` contradicting the settings are still refused;
- the solvers of hypre compute where its memory is (on the host if hypre is
  built without GPU support); `HypreEuclid` and `HypreParaSails` compute on
  the host; PETSc is refused with the linear solvers on the GPU; the
  location of the preconditioners is only checked for the known names;
- the preconditioner `None` gave no preconditioner but a failure with an
  empty message (existing defect);
- the settings are read before the initialization of MPI, which is
  finalized if the request of hypre on the host is refused; a missing value
  of an option is refused; `--hypre-device-pool-size` is refused with
  `--execution cpu`;
- documentation of the real limits of the placements.

Copies of the arrays of the materials between the host and the device:
counted (numbers, bytes, time, in each direction) by the accesses of
`MaterialArrays` when the accessed copy was not valid, including the new
`read` and `readTangentOperatorBlocks` used by the kernels
(`getMaterialArraysTransfers`), and printed after the profiling table.

Behaviour libraries for both processors: CMake function
`mfem_mgis_add_behaviours_library` (module `MFEMMGISBehaviours.cmake`,
installed and loaded by the configuration file) building the libraries for
the CPU (generic interface) and, if MFEM uses a GPU, for the GPU
(generic-parallel interface, cuda or hip backend), under
`<target>/cpu` and `<target>/gpu`; `getBehavioursLibrary` returns the one
placed by the execution settings.

ExecutionSettingsTest: libraries built by the CMake function, a library of
the generic-parallel interface for the host used when the behaviours are on
the CPU, `--execution cpu --device debug`, environment variables ignored,
preconditioners `None` and `HypreEuclid`, copies of the arrays (none on the
host, both directions between processors), GPU variants only with the
library for the GPU (31 variants). Mutations of each fix and of the
counting are detected. Suites: CPU 196/196, GPU 209/211 (the 2 expected
failures), device tests 94/94.
